mb|3C|an|second suit, five cards|
pg| ***** 3 ***** |


mb|P|mb|4S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|5D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I disagree with 5@D. Partner wants to play 4 spades so you should honor that request. In fact, I would think about 6 with 2 spades, running diamonds and a heart void. You can pass which is reasonable or bid 6@S which is not a bad gamble.|
PG| ***** 4 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Further, you don't need to play exclusion blackwood on this hand. Partner must have great spades so at worst you are missing one key card and probably none other than @HA. Having said that, I don't like 4@S bid by West but it is acceptable. I will explain after the play.|
PG| ***** 5 ***** |


ub||
PG| ***** 6 ***** |


mb|6S|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 7 ***** |


