Hand 3
http://tinyurl.com/2cv4vb4j
qx|A3|st||rh||ah|Board 3 IMPs   -   February 21, 2024|pn|hondo717,Eliza42,ashhoki,ladydoc|
md|1S654HT9643D82CJ83,SQHAKJ8752DAJ543C,SKT83HDT6CAKQT752,SAJ972HQDKQ97C964|sv|e|
mb|P|mb|1H|mb|4C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Interesting choices for North. A case can be made for 2@C, 3@C, 4@C, and even 5@C. Double is even possible because it is conceivable that 4@S is a good contract. However preempting in clubs with such a nice suit is a better way to compete than making a takeout double. I like his choice.|
PG| ***** 45 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
mb|D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now let me discuss what the double means in this sequence. It is NOT a pure penalty double per se. On this auction, it is fairly unlikely that East holds enough clubs to make a penalty double. It is a ^*BCard Showing^*n double. |
PG| ***** 46 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It says "partner this is our hand. I have some values. Do something intelligent." That is why I nickname it the ^*BDo Something Intelligent Double^*n. Often partner will pass although that is not mandatory. |
PG| ***** 47 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|On this hand in fact, I think West has an obvious pull to 4@H.|
PG| ***** 48 ***** |


mb|P|mb|4H|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East should pass. The @HQ is a nice card and partner has at least 6 nice hearts with no great defense.|
PG| ***** 49 ***** |


mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 50 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|CK|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I guess North leads K from AK. That is fine and actually what I prefer but it is old fashioned since you can't differentiate between holdings AK and KQ. Actually on this hand, from AKQ you lead the Q. It doesn't matter.|
PG| ***** 51 ***** |


